   "id": "b2-19",
   "name": "Experiment 5: the conditions needed for germination"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Aim: to show that seeds need water, oxygen and warmth to germinate.\nSet up four test tubes, each with a few soaked bean seeds:\n• A: moist cotton wool, open to the air, warm room (the control: every condition present);\n• B: dry cotton wool, warm room (no water);\n• C: seeds covered with boiled and cooled water and a layer of oil on top (no oxygen);\n• D: moist cotton wool, in a refrigerator (no warmth).\nLeave them for about a week.\nResults: only the seeds in A germinate.\nConclusion: seeds need water, oxygen and a suitable temperature. Each tube lacks one condition: comparing it with A shows that condition is needed.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "t": "C"
  },
  "problem": "Why is the water in tube {t} boiled, and why is oil poured on top?",
  "steps": [
   "Boiling drives the dissolved air (oxygen) out of the water.",
   "The layer of oil stops air from dissolving back in.",
   "So tube {t} has water and warmth but no oxygen."
  ],
  "answer": "To remove oxygen and keep it out, so the tube tests whether oxygen is needed.",
  "checks": []
 },
